{"author":{"id":"ce771b8a9b8c30a8aac165a8b1cdb0957637d3941276ec4f27335daee16d79de"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794857396,"nonce":"+mmbHf15DZERKc3kbUD5Ws4c6M4=","title":"The app still models a catalogue world that one grower never uses: a strain","message":"database with 15 bundled third-party records and their licence paperwork, a\nseed bank with germination logs, grow spaces with an equipment catalogue\n(lights, tents, fans), and bundled equipment presets. Each of these adds\nnavigation, forms and maintenance the single-grower diary does not earn, and\nthe bundled data drags a permanent provenance and licence obligation behind a\nsigned binary.\n\n\nStrip back to the grow. The grow itself carries everything the removed\nfeatures used to supply: a free-text **Strain label**, a **Photoperiod** /\n**Autoflower** toggle, heat/cold/light tolerances and lamp facts (real wall\nwatts, dimmable) grouped in an Advanced Settings section. Home Assistant\nentities enter the app only as per-grow **Bindings**; grow spaces and the\nequipment catalogue disappear, and the seed bank goes without a replacement.\nA single migration hard-drops the removed tables, deriving each surviving\ngrow's label and photoperiod from its former strain link.\n\n\n1. As a grower, I want to record the cultivar name as free text on a grow, so that I can remember what I grew without maintaining a catalogue.\n2. As a grower, I want to mark a grow Photoperiod or Autoflower, so that the harvest forecast estimates the flip correctly.\n3. As a grower, I want sensible default flowering windows from the toggle alone, so that the forecast works with minimal input.\n4. As a grower, I want the tuning knobs collected in an Advanced Settings section on the grow, so that the daily flow stays simple.\n5. As a grower, I want to set heat, cold and light tolerance per grow, so that environment alert thresholds match the plant I am actually growing.\n6. As a grower, I want tolerance settings to default to Average, so that a new grow needs no tuning to be sensible.\n7. As a grower, I want to enter real wall watts and whether the lamp is dimmable on the grow, so that lamp-height advice reflects my actual lamp.\n8. As a grower, I want the lamp advisor to fall back to its 330 W default when watts are unset, so that advice never blocks on a form field.\n9. As a grower, I want to bind Home Assistant sensor entities directly to a grow by Role, so that sensors work without inventing equipment records first.\n10. As a grower, I want live tiles and environment charts to keep reading from Bindings, so that everything I rely on keeps working.\n11. As a grower, I want the light staircase chart to keep working from the light Role, so that I can still see the Light Cycle.\n12. As a grower, I want yields grouped by Strain label in cross-grow history, so that I can compare cultivars across grows.\n13. As a grower, I want \"start next run\" to carry the Strain label and photoperiod, so that the new grow starts informed.\n14. As a grower, I want phase picks to record Flip 12/12 for Photoperiod grows and a generic phase change for Autoflower grows, so that the event log stays accurate.\n15. As a grower, I want my existing grows to keep their strain name and photoperiod after upgrading, so that the migration does not rewrite my history.\n16. As a grower, I want the app to work with zero equipment records, so that Bindings are the only sensor concept I must understand.\n17. As a grower, I no longer see Strains, Seedbank, Spaces or Equipment in the navigation, so that the app shows only what I use.\n18. As a grower, I want onboarding reduced to binding sensors and creating the grow, so that setup takes a minute.\n19. As a grower, I want the strain fields inline in the grow-creation step of onboarding, so that I can still record what I am growing without a wizard detour.\n20. As a grower, I want the lamp advisor card on the grow overview to keep working, so that I keep the advice I had.\n21. As a maintainer, I want the bundled strain and equipment data deleted, so that the third-party licence and provenance burden disappears from the codebase.\n22. As a maintainer, I want the removed features' tables dropped by migration, so that the schema matches what the app actually does.\n23. As the operator, I accept losing seed batches, germination logs, spaces and equipment rows on upgrade, so that the app strips clean; the `/data` backup taken before upgrading is the record.\n24. As a maintainer, I want the yield write-back endpoint removed, so that no feature dead-ends against the deleted catalogue.\n\n\n- **Grow model** gains `strain_label` (free text), a photoperiod toggle\n  (Photoperiod / Autoflower), `heat_tolerance` / `cold_tolerance` /\n  `light_tolerance` (Sensitive / Average / Tolerant, default Average),\n  `real_watts` (nullable) and `dimmable` (default true). The UI groups the\n  tolerances plus the lamp facts in an Advanced Settings section on the grow.\n- **Removed features**: the strain catalogue (CRUD, clone-as-phenotype,\n  bundled read-only rules, bundled strain data and its seeder), the seed bank\n  (batches and germination tests, including the plant-start decrement), grow\n  spaces (space CRUD, the space–equipment link, the space step in onboarding,\n  the space-seeded binding defaults), and the equipment catalogue (item CRUD,\n  bundled equipment presets and their seeder). Sensor equipment items dissolve\n  into the existing per-grow Bindings; the grow page keeps its binding\n  pickers as the only sensor entry point.\n- **Engines keep their logic, change their source**: forecast, feed-fit and\n  the phase picker read the photoperiod from the grow (default windows\n  unchanged: photoperiod 56–77 flowering days, autos 63–77 total days); the\n  environment threshold shifts read the grow's tolerances; the lamp advisor\n  reads the grow's watts and dimmable flag with the 330 W fallback when\n  unset. The photoperiod-vs-auto distinction drives the phase picker's\n  Flip 12/12 branch.\n- **History**: the yield aggregate keys on Strain label (unlabelled grows\n  group together); the yield write-back is deleted; \"start next run\" copies\n  the label and photoperiod instead of a strain reference.\n- **Migration**: one new versioned migration hard-drops the strain, seed\n  batch, germination log, grow space, space–equipment and equipment tables\n  plus the dead grow columns, and derives each surviving grow's Strain label\n  and photoperiod from its former strain link; tolerances default to Average.\n  Migration history stays append-only — earlier migrations are never edited.\n- **Navigation and onboarding**: nav entries for Strains, Seedbank, Spaces\n  and Equipment are removed; onboarding collapses to two steps — bind\n  sensors, then create the grow (strain fields inline) with plants.\n- **Docs**: SPEC sections for equipment/strain/seedbank/viability and the\n  affected acceptance criteria are rewritten; AGENTS.md's strain and\n  equipment clauses shrink; THREAT-MODEL R3 (strain source link) closes.\n  DECISIONS.md D075 already records the decision and its supersessions.\n- **mock-HA is unchanged**: sensors plus the light entity keep exercising\n  Bindings, auto-log and the light staircase.\n- The non-negotiables are untouched: ingress-correct relative URLs, SI\n  storage with HA-unit display, no telemetry, the lint block, and the\n  supervisor-token rules (no new service calls are introduced).\n\n\n- Good tests assert external behaviour — HTTP responses, migration outcomes,\n  rendered UI — never internal call graphs. Existing seams only; the spec\n  introduces none.\n- **Migration seam** (prior art: the bundled-ID upgrade test): seed a\n  pre-migration fixture database with grows linked to strains, run the new\n  migration, and assert the surviving grows carry derived label and\n  photoperiod, tolerances default to Average, the removed tables and columns\n  are gone, and the app still boots.\n- **Backend HTTP API seam** (prior art: the existing API integration suite):\n  grow create/update round-trips the new fields; removed routes answer 404;\n  environment, lamp, forecast, feed-fit and history responses reflect\n  grow-sourced inputs; next-run carries label and photoperiod; the yield\n  aggregate groups by label.\n- **E2E Playwright seam** (prior art: the onboarding and forms specs): the\n  two-step wizard works; Advanced Settings renders on the grow form; the\n  removed nav entries are absent; the grow list survives the vanished\n  endpoints.\n- Core unit tests: the tolerance-shift and photoperiod-forecast tests are\n  re-sourced from grow inputs; deleted modules' tests are removed with them.\n\n\n- Any new capability: no strain import/export, no CSV, no per-strain\n  flowering-day overrides.\n- Exporting the removed features' data (the `/data` backup is the record).\n- Rollback tooling for the migration; recovery is restore-from-backup.\n- Feed templates and the substrate science-pack presets (untouched).\n- Everything already out of scope for v1 (multi-user, cloud sync, sharing,\n  automatic device control).\n\n\n- Decision record: D075 in docs/DECISIONS.md; it supersedes D012, D014,\n  D015, D043, D044, D045, D049, D050, D051, D052, D053, D056 and D067.\n- Glossary already updated: Photoperiod and Autoflower are grow attributes,\n  Strain label is a term, Light Cycle is framed on the grow.\n- This is a breaking release (next minor version bumps); the upgrade note\n  must tell the operator to back up `/data` first.\n- The removed routes disappear from the ingress rewrite list too.\n- Prose lint (vale) applies to all rewritten docs and UI strings.","files":null}]}